# Prettier does not read .gitignore, so generated and byte-compared files are
# listed here by hand. Formatting anything below is at best noise and at worst
# a broken build.

# Generated output.
.next/
out/
build/
android/build/
android/*/build/
android/.gradle/

# drizzle-kit owns these: the migration SQL and the snapshot JSON it diffs
# against. Reformatting a snapshot is how you get a migration that regenerates
# itself (see `npm run db:generate`).
drizzle/

# `npm test` compares these byte for byte against
# `JSON.stringify(snapshot, null, 2) + "\n"` — that is the whole point of them,
# and it is how a change to the shape clients receive gets noticed. Prettier
# would rewrite all nine and the suite would fail until `npm run contract:emit`
# put them back, which the next prettier run would undo again.
contract/fixtures/

# The extracted rule text is a verbatim copy of Bandai's manual; the arena
# engine cites section numbers into it by line.
docs/rules/

# Markdown is left alone deliberately, and this is the one opinionated entry
# here. Prettier pads every table cell out to the width of the longest cell in
# its column, which turns the data-source and decision tables in CLAUDE.md and
# the arena specs into single lines over 1,500 characters — unreadable in the
# source, and a whole-table diff every time one word changes. It also rewrites
# *emphasis* to _emphasis_ throughout for no gain. These documents are prose
# that gets read and hand-edited far more often than the code does, and the
# formatting they have is deliberate.
*.md

# Not tracked; belongs to the local Claude Code setup, not the project.
.claude/
